desc: Number each line (1. 2. 3. etc)
category: manual
par: 16
hint1: A put command with expression, or a macro
hint2: g Ctrl-A in visual block mode creates sequential numbers starting from a base
solution: :%s/^/0. <CR>gg<C-V>Gg<C-A>
note: Prefix every line with '0. '; select the 0 column with <C-V>, then g<C-A>
note: increments each selected number sequentially (1, 2, 3, ...).
--- START ---
apple
banana
cherry
date
elderberry
fig
grape
--- GOAL ---
1. apple
2. banana
3. cherry
4. date
5. elderberry
6. fig
7. grape
--- END ---
